# Depot Design System Rules

When creating or modifying Phoenix HEEX templates, components, or styles in this project:

- **Theme**: Dark server-rack developer console. Base background is Carbon (`bg-carbon` / `#04040b`).
- **Surfaces**:
  - Cards / Content panels: Graphite (`bg-graphite` / `#121113`).
  - Nested elements / Footer: Obsidian (`bg-obsidian` / `#1a191b`).
  - Dividers and borders: 1px hairline Basalt (`border-basalt` / `#2b292d`).
- **Elevation**:
  - NO drop shadows (`shadow-md`, `shadow-lg`).
  - Use 1px Basalt hairline borders and optional top highlight (`shadow-subtle`).
- **CTA Discipline**:
  - Signal Green (`bg-signal-green` / `#71d083`) is reserved **only** for the single primary CTA button fill.
  - Secondary buttons must be ghost/outline: `border-basalt text-ash hover:border-pewter`.
- **Border Radius**:
  - `rounded-md` (6px) for cards, buttons, inputs.
  - `rounded-xs` (2px) for tags, badges, nav items.
  - Never use large radii (12px+, pill shapes).
- **Typography**:
  - Headings: Red Hat Display (`font-display`) with negative tracking (`tracking-[-0.025em]`), color Chalk (`text-chalk`).
  - Body: Red Hat Text (`font-text`) with positive tracking (`tracking-[0.025em]`), color Ash (`text-ash`).
  - Code/Status: Red Hat Mono (`font-mono`), color Ash/Silver with status dots (`bg-signal-green`).
  - Never use pure white (`#ffffff`).
- Reference `DESIGN.md` in the project root for full design details.
